                <pb facs="1031" n="911" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg911"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.77/2635: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Warren</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-08-15T17:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 15,
                                1922—5 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>91. No objection is perceived to the suggestion of the Japanese Government as set
                    forth in the last paragraph of your 135, August 9, 1 p.m. Presumably it will be
                    embodied in the formal reply of the Japanese Government whereupon the Department
                    will be prepared to submit it to the other Powers concerned.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
